1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:02,280
This series was created
for entertainment purposes.

2
00:00:02,310 --> 00:00:05,758
The characters, actions, locations,
dialogue, glanguages, ceremonies,

3
00:00:05,794 --> 00:00:10,100
and artistic elements depicted in this series
are fictional and based on imagination,

4
00:00:10,130 --> 00:00:13,976
incorporating the beauty
of the region’s diverse cultures,

5
00:00:14,011 --> 00:00:18,447
including those of Lanna,
Myanmar, Tai ethnic, and China.

6
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:20,567
It is not intended to disrespect
any history,

7
00:00:20,598 --> 00:00:23,662
ethnic group, organization, profession,
or group of individuals.

8
00:00:23,690 --> 00:00:25,970
Viewer discretion is advised.

9
00:00:37,152 --> 00:00:38,380
I am Na Boon.

10
00:00:38,845 --> 00:00:40,598
I lost my father when I was very young.

11
00:00:41,120 --> 00:00:44,402
And just recently, I lost my mother, too.

12
00:00:52,951 --> 00:00:54,398
I am Fong Nuan.

13
00:00:54,690 --> 00:00:59,241
Since birth, I’ve drawn breath,
yet never truly felt alive.

14
00:00:59,583 --> 00:01:01,640
Okay. I’m coming. Hold on.

15
00:01:02,056 --> 00:01:03,035
Oops, I’m sorry.

16
00:01:03,068 --> 00:01:04,240
Really sorry.

17
00:01:08,382 --> 00:01:11,699
If this suffering
is the result of my karma,

18
00:01:11,950 --> 00:01:17,998
I humbly ask for forgiveness
for my deeds in past lives and this one.

19
00:01:27,290 --> 00:01:28,496
I have no siblings.

20
00:01:28,890 --> 00:01:31,102
My best friend betrayed me.

21
00:01:32,186 --> 00:01:34,200
My boyfriend stabbed me in the back.

22
00:01:35,068 --> 00:01:37,290
Is this the karma
I’ve brought upon myself?

23
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:40,780
Please grant me a new life,

24
00:01:41,087 --> 00:01:44,100
with the strength to do as I wish,

25
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:48,402
to go wherever I desire,

26
00:01:49,354 --> 00:01:51,142
and to truly live,

27
00:01:51,179 --> 00:01:55,000
rather than spend my days
merely awaiting death.

28
00:01:55,930 --> 00:01:58,782
I don’t know what I’ve done
to deserve all this,

29
00:01:59,985 --> 00:02:01,902
but I’m begging for forgiveness,

30
00:02:02,422 --> 00:02:06,296
for whatever I did
in my past lives or this one.

31
00:02:07,140 --> 00:02:10,201
Please, let fate be kind to me.

32
00:02:10,785 --> 00:02:13,180
Don’t make me suffer any more
than I already have.

33
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:03,097
What the heck?

34
00:06:45,853 --> 00:06:47,090
How did you get in here?!

35
00:06:48,331 --> 00:06:48,770
I…

36
00:06:48,804 --> 00:06:50,000
Well, I…

37
00:06:50,040 --> 00:06:53,502
Did you sneak in to see our
<i>“Liang Phee Khun Nam”</i> ceremony?
[The ceremony to honor the water spirits]

38
00:06:54,168 --> 00:06:55,176
Hey!

39
00:06:55,918 --> 00:06:56,930
Don’t come any closer!

40
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:03,299
How dare you point a stick at the prince?

41
00:07:03,590 --> 00:07:04,601
Prince?

42
00:07:06,525 --> 00:07:07,290
Fong Nuan.

43
00:07:09,066 --> 00:07:10,400
How did you get in here, little sister?

44
00:07:10,952 --> 00:07:11,822
No, no, no!

45
00:07:11,854 --> 00:07:13,081
I don’t have any siblings.

46
00:07:13,106 --> 00:07:14,130
I’m an only child.

47
00:07:16,250 --> 00:07:17,051
Soldiers!

48
00:07:17,442 --> 00:07:18,100
Seize her!

49
00:07:18,130 --> 00:07:18,900
Yes, Your Highness.

50
00:07:18,930 --> 00:07:19,802
Do not!

51
00:07:21,910 --> 00:07:23,200
She is with me.

52
00:07:23,931 --> 00:07:24,998
Let me handle her.

53
00:09:50,311 --> 00:09:51,200
Fong Nuan.

54
00:09:55,675 --> 00:09:56,802
How are you faring?

55
00:09:57,352 --> 00:10:00,402
Do you still have a headache?

56
00:10:02,048 --> 00:10:04,402
You really couldn’t be any more stubborn.

57
00:10:05,014 --> 00:10:07,601
Why did you enter
the ceremony to honor the water spirits?

58
00:10:08,311 --> 00:10:09,490
Weren’t you afraid?

59
00:10:10,365 --> 00:10:11,198
Uh…

60
00:10:13,238 --> 00:10:14,380
Fong Nuan?

61
00:10:15,371 --> 00:10:17,700
Who is Fong Nuan?

62
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:20,600
Do you think doing this

63
00:10:21,180 --> 00:10:23,770
will make me any less angry with you
for sneaking into the ceremony?

64
00:10:25,672 --> 00:10:29,690
Do you not know that women are forbidden
from attending sacred ceremonies?

65
00:10:30,730 --> 00:10:32,002
Uh… I…

66
00:10:32,349 --> 00:10:35,977
I don’t know how I came here.

67
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:39,032
And that ceremony thing,
I have no idea how I popped up there.

68
00:10:39,059 --> 00:10:41,170
I woke up, and suddenly, I was just there.

69
00:10:42,110 --> 00:10:43,065
So…

70
00:10:44,499 --> 00:10:46,100
Sis, will you tell me…

71
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:50,840
who I am?

72
00:10:59,970 --> 00:11:01,400
Your name is Fong Nuan.

73
00:11:01,997 --> 00:11:03,400
My name is Maneethip.

74
00:11:04,410 --> 00:11:06,299
We’re both from Wang Nam Lin.

75
00:11:06,850 --> 00:11:09,271
Your father was
my father’s younger brother.

76
00:11:09,616 --> 00:11:13,810
Your parents died when you were young,
so you’ve been living with me ever since.

77
00:11:14,690 --> 00:11:17,102
We’re like real sisters,
born to the same mother.

78
00:11:18,230 --> 00:11:20,880
Do you truly not remember,
or are you just teasing me?

79
00:11:24,853 --> 00:11:25,601
Then…

80
00:11:27,004 --> 00:11:28,395
Where are we?

81
00:11:30,096 --> 00:11:31,096
Ullavee.

82
00:11:32,891 --> 00:11:34,770
We moved to Ullavee a long time ago.

83
00:11:36,820 --> 00:11:37,997
Ullavee?

84
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:39,994
ULLAVEE: THE FORBIDDEN KINGDOM

85
00:11:40,013 --> 00:11:43,410
Ullavee, an ancient forbidden kingdom.

86
00:11:43,678 --> 00:11:45,998
Its exact age has yet to be determined.

87
00:11:46,034 --> 00:11:47,170
It was only recently discovered.

88
00:11:49,020 --> 00:11:51,930
Ullavee was known as a tributary kingdom,

89
00:11:52,125 --> 00:11:58,640
caught between three major powers:
Lanna, China, and Myanmar.

90
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:02,899
Though small, Ullavee was a kingdom
that no one wanted to go to war with,

91
00:12:03,266 --> 00:12:05,161
as it was a center of trade.

92
00:12:05,190 --> 00:12:08,900
It was wealthy, with abundant gemstones
and rich deposits of natural minerals.

93
00:12:11,188 --> 00:12:13,000
These are the ruins of Wiang Kaew,

94
00:12:13,720 --> 00:12:16,497
once the royal grounds of Ullavee’s king.

95
00:12:17,437 --> 00:12:20,802
However,
these accounts remain speculative,

96
00:12:21,328 --> 00:12:24,930
based on historical records,
stories, and folklore.

97
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:27,640
They haven’t been conclusively proven.

98
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:30,899
According to records
from neighboring cities,

99
00:12:31,280 --> 00:12:35,099
Ullavee’s last king was a very cruel man.

100
00:12:36,229 --> 00:12:39,210
He killed his own siblings
to seize the throne.

101
00:12:42,310 --> 00:12:45,000
People were so afraid of him
that they didn’t dare talk about him.

102
00:12:45,170 --> 00:12:50,097
That’s why we don’t have
many historical records about Ullavee.

103
00:12:51,376 --> 00:12:54,650
Oh, and the project will be called
“The Forbidden, Hidden Kingdom.”

104
00:12:54,928 --> 00:13:00,080
The client wants both the exhibition
and the full audiovisual show.

105
00:13:00,970 --> 00:13:02,200
Let’s work hard on this, guys.

106
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:11,320
Here, Na Boon.

107
00:13:12,112 --> 00:13:13,602
The books about Ullavee.

108
00:13:16,088 --> 00:13:17,370
If you need more resources,

109
00:13:17,900 --> 00:13:19,402
I can recommend some libraries.

110
00:13:19,690 --> 00:13:22,777
But books about Ullavee
are hard to come by.

111
00:13:31,242 --> 00:13:32,798
Ullavee.

112
00:13:34,860 --> 00:13:35,899
Ullavee?

113
00:13:37,034 --> 00:13:38,377
Have you gone bananas, Boon?

114
00:13:39,010 --> 00:13:41,050
Will you stop speaking so strangely?

115
00:13:41,782 --> 00:13:43,000
Tell me at once.

116
00:13:43,216 --> 00:13:45,500
Why did you enter
the <i>“Liang Phee Khun Nam”</i> ceremony?

117
00:13:49,130 --> 00:13:50,100
No.

118
00:13:51,096 --> 00:13:52,699
Something must have gone wrong.

119
00:13:54,524 --> 00:13:55,770
The medicine is ready, Your Highness.

120
00:14:00,800 --> 00:14:01,800
Eva!

121
00:14:26,005 --> 00:14:26,899
Come on in.

122
00:14:29,090 --> 00:14:30,004
So…

123
00:14:30,961 --> 00:14:34,900
Bew, are you sure Boon won’t show up
to surprise you for your birthday?

124
00:14:36,370 --> 00:14:37,182
Come on.

125
00:14:38,668 --> 00:14:40,560
Boon said she had
a big project in Chiang Mai.

126
00:14:40,590 --> 00:14:41,601
She won’t bother us.

127
00:14:45,768 --> 00:14:47,699
I’ll go change, then we can celebrate.

128
00:14:57,120 --> 00:14:57,863
Boon…

129
00:15:09,533 --> 00:15:10,902
How could you do this to me?

130
00:15:11,407 --> 00:15:12,890
How could you?!

131
00:15:12,961 --> 00:15:14,754
This is all your setup, right?

132
00:15:14,780 --> 00:15:16,930
You’re just messing with me,
aren’t you, Eva?

133
00:15:17,444 --> 00:15:18,520
Who is Eva, my lady?

134
00:15:19,410 --> 00:15:21,000
I am Lha, my lady.

135
00:15:22,285 --> 00:15:23,398
Lha who?

136
00:15:24,265 --> 00:15:25,853
This isn’t funny, Eva.

137
00:15:25,880 --> 00:15:26,749
Fong Nuan.

138
00:15:27,389 --> 00:15:29,400
What are you talking about?
I don’t understand.

139
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:30,801
Who is Eva?

140
00:15:31,100 --> 00:15:32,602
It’s her! Eva!

141
00:15:33,377 --> 00:15:39,040
I am Lha, a servant to Princess Maneethip
and you, Lady Fong Nuan.

142
00:15:41,190 --> 00:15:42,100
Fong Nuan.

143
00:15:44,377 --> 00:15:45,570
What are you guys playing at?

144
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:46,782
-Lady Fong Nuan!
-Fong Nuan!

145
00:15:47,050 --> 00:15:47,949
Lady Fong Nuan!

146
00:15:47,986 --> 00:15:48,900
Fong Nuan!

147
00:15:49,502 --> 00:15:50,377
Lady Fong Nuan!

148
00:16:04,217 --> 00:16:05,200
Lady Fong Nuan.

149
00:16:08,620 --> 00:16:09,400
Fong Nuan.

150
00:16:12,558 --> 00:16:13,601
Lady Fong Nuan.

151
00:16:22,170 --> 00:16:23,890
Sis, where is this place?

152
00:16:26,062 --> 00:16:27,170
Ullavee, my lady.

153
00:16:27,524 --> 00:16:28,400
Shit.

154
00:16:33,760 --> 00:16:36,200
(Ullavee, an ancient forbidden kingdom.)

155
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:39,220
(Its exact age has yet to be determined.)

156
00:16:39,250 --> 00:16:40,361
(It was only recently discovered.)

157
00:16:42,631 --> 00:16:43,398
Fong Nuan!

158
00:16:43,539 --> 00:16:44,400
Lady Fong Nuan!

159
00:16:45,647 --> 00:16:47,128
(These are the ruins of Wiang Kaew,)

160
00:16:47,160 --> 00:16:49,798
(once the royal grounds
of Ullavee’s king.)

161
00:16:50,240 --> 00:16:51,250
Lady Fong Nuan!

162
00:16:51,900 --> 00:16:52,700
Fong Nuan!

163
00:16:59,631 --> 00:17:00,730
Lady Fong Nuan!

164
00:17:01,518 --> 00:17:02,382
Lady Fong Nuan!

165
00:17:20,167 --> 00:17:21,900
You said it was a forbidden kingdom.

166
00:17:22,499 --> 00:17:23,801
What made it forbidden?

167
00:17:24,062 --> 00:17:26,380
(No one could enter or leave.)

168
00:17:34,810 --> 00:17:36,302
-Lady Fong Nuan!
-My goodness!

169
00:17:37,028 --> 00:17:37,802
Lady Fong Nuan!

170
00:17:38,786 --> 00:17:39,699
Lady Fong Nuan.

171
00:17:42,525 --> 00:17:43,530
Lady Fong Nuan.

172
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:34,400
Fong Nuan.

173
00:19:35,438 --> 00:19:36,970
How did you get in here, little sister?

174
00:19:37,623 --> 00:19:38,850
Where is this place?

175
00:19:39,112 --> 00:19:40,097
Ullavee.

176
00:19:41,613 --> 00:19:42,703
Ullavee?

177
00:19:43,558 --> 00:19:45,080
(Ullavee, an ancient forbidden kingdom.)

178
00:19:45,110 --> 00:19:47,457
(Its exact age has yet to be determined.)

179
00:19:47,488 --> 00:19:48,490
(It was only recently discovered.)

180
00:19:51,331 --> 00:19:52,697
Your name is Fong Nuan.

181
00:19:53,114 --> 00:19:54,080
Fong Nuan?

182
00:19:55,080 --> 00:19:56,097
Na Boon?

183
00:19:56,762 --> 00:19:57,850
Who is Eva, my lady?

184
00:19:58,762 --> 00:20:00,250
I am Lha, my lady.

185
00:20:01,094 --> 00:20:01,998
Lha?

186
00:20:02,740 --> 00:20:03,598
Eva?

187
00:20:07,149 --> 00:20:08,499
How are all these connected?

188
00:20:09,414 --> 00:20:10,797
Is this a parallel universe?

189
00:20:12,262 --> 00:20:13,800
But this is Ullavee.

190
00:20:16,432 --> 00:20:17,700
What am I doing here?

191
00:20:20,690 --> 00:20:21,897
I need to find a way back.

192
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:23,447
A way back.

193
00:20:23,850 --> 00:20:25,180
A way back.

194
00:20:57,284 --> 00:20:58,100
Fong Nuan!

195
00:21:01,040 --> 00:21:01,706
Gosh!

196
00:21:01,737 --> 00:21:02,600
Fong Nuan!

197
00:21:02,640 --> 00:21:03,945
-Argh!
-Fong Nuan!

198
00:21:29,740 --> 00:21:30,690
Are you all right?

199
00:21:31,751 --> 00:21:32,800
Are you hurt anywhere?

200
00:21:34,595 --> 00:21:36,000
I almost got hurt because of you.

201
00:21:36,450 --> 00:21:37,897
You suddenly barged in.

202
00:21:38,550 --> 00:21:39,801
You scared me.

203
00:21:40,540 --> 00:21:43,355
I was the one whose heart nearly stopped.

204
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:46,100
Fong Nuan, what’s the matter with you?

205
00:21:47,197 --> 00:21:48,400
What were you thinking?

206
00:21:48,780 --> 00:21:50,402
Do you ever think about me?

207
00:21:51,800 --> 00:21:55,182
If anything happened to you,
what would I do?

208
00:21:57,970 --> 00:21:58,899
I’m sorry.

209
00:22:02,790 --> 00:22:05,974
Don’t you ever do that again.

210
00:22:07,450 --> 00:22:08,997
I have only you.

211
00:22:10,768 --> 00:22:11,980
Do not leave me.

212
00:22:37,200 --> 00:22:41,090
PRINCE MUEANG FAH

213
00:22:52,057 --> 00:22:53,210
It’s just me, Mueang Fah.

214
00:22:55,400 --> 00:22:56,389
PRINCE INDRARAJA

215
00:22:56,410 --> 00:22:58,700
Father already knew
I would bring you before him.

216
00:22:59,850 --> 00:23:02,210
The first time in life
granted an audience with Father.

217
00:23:03,334 --> 00:23:04,200
I’m happy for you.

218
00:23:07,010 --> 00:23:08,840
With your suppression of the rebellion
at the border,

219
00:23:08,870 --> 00:23:10,272
Father is very pleased.

220
00:23:11,500 --> 00:23:15,580
Should he ask,
I trust you’ll know what to say.

221
00:23:18,102 --> 00:23:20,377
“I merely followed
the orders of the Crown Prince,”

222
00:23:22,780 --> 00:23:23,979
“Prince Indraraja.”

223
00:23:25,808 --> 00:23:26,600
Very good.

224
00:23:27,037 --> 00:23:28,650
And your success was made possible

225
00:23:28,678 --> 00:23:34,090
with the aid of Crown Prince Pha Wiang
of Merng Mang.

226
00:23:35,588 --> 00:23:36,502
I will not forget it.

227
00:23:38,520 --> 00:23:39,401
Pha Wiang,

228
00:23:40,296 --> 00:23:42,260
do you see now that
my younger brother Mueang Fah

229
00:23:42,290 --> 00:23:44,650
is neither arrogant nor ambitious?

230
00:23:45,460 --> 00:23:47,802
He is honest and a man of his word.

231
00:23:50,730 --> 00:23:52,397
I, too, shall appear before the King.

232
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,299
I wish to hear it with my own ears.

233
00:23:55,600 --> 00:23:58,897
If you honor our agreement,
then you will earn my trust.

234
00:23:59,751 --> 00:24:04,001
Your trust is worth less than my dignity.

235
00:24:05,560 --> 00:24:07,183
I will honor our agreement

236
00:24:07,940 --> 00:24:09,250
because I keep my word,

237
00:24:10,990 --> 00:24:13,176
not because I seek anyone’s approval.

238
00:24:13,220 --> 00:24:14,600
Are you talking back to me?

239
00:24:17,060 --> 00:24:18,320
We’re all on the same side here.

240
00:24:18,350 --> 00:24:19,900
No need to turn against each other.

241
00:24:25,597 --> 00:24:27,210
If you do as I say,

242
00:24:29,550 --> 00:24:31,297
you’ll be allowed to reside in Ullavee.

243
00:24:31,990 --> 00:24:33,000
I promise.

244
00:24:50,120 --> 00:24:54,370
PRINCE KONG TAI / PRINCE FAH HAAM

245
00:24:54,400 --> 00:24:55,697
ROYAL CONSORT SUKANTHA / PRINCE JOM HARN

246
00:24:55,730 --> 00:24:56,598
Jom Harn,

247
00:24:57,940 --> 00:25:00,497
did you know Mueang Fah
was granted an audience with the King?

248
00:25:01,990 --> 00:25:03,500
Everyone in Wiang Kaew knows.

249
00:25:03,952 --> 00:25:05,299
How could I not?

250
00:25:05,980 --> 00:25:07,801
I’m glad Brother is here.

251
00:25:08,305 --> 00:25:09,870
It’s been so long since I last saw him.

252
00:25:09,900 --> 00:25:10,899
I’ve missed him.

253
00:25:12,392 --> 00:25:14,270
You may miss him, but don’t go near him,

254
00:25:14,801 --> 00:25:16,238
and never bring him to our residence.

255
00:25:16,720 --> 00:25:18,397
He will bring calamity upon us.

256
00:25:22,840 --> 00:25:24,228
ROYAL CONSORT CHIANG LA-OR

257
00:25:24,260 --> 00:25:26,500
I bow before you, Royal Consort Sukantha.

258
00:25:26,620 --> 00:25:28,902
I bow before you,
Royal Consort Chiang La-or.

259
00:25:30,522 --> 00:25:31,400
Hongkham.

260
00:25:32,241 --> 00:25:33,370
You’re here as well?

261
00:25:45,835 --> 00:25:48,001
Those of the outer court
have royal duties to attend to.

262
00:25:48,297 --> 00:25:49,890
Such matters are no concern
of the inner court.

263
00:25:50,374 --> 00:25:53,280
Government affairs are no place for women.

264
00:25:58,665 --> 00:26:01,000
Then why are you here,
Royal Consort  Sukantha?

265
00:26:01,188 --> 00:26:03,000
We are both women, are we not?

266
00:26:04,320 --> 00:26:06,696
The King permits me and your mother

267
00:26:07,370 --> 00:26:09,672
to attend an audience
whenever matters of importance arise.

268
00:26:09,700 --> 00:26:11,000
Everyone knows that.

269
00:26:11,840 --> 00:26:16,000
Father has also allowed me
to attend and broaden my knowledge.

270
00:26:16,031 --> 00:26:16,608
PRINCESS HONGKHAM

271
00:26:16,608 --> 00:26:19,970
After all, I am his eldest daughter.
PRINCESS HONGKHAM

272
00:26:20,320 --> 00:26:22,250
Just because I am not a man

273
00:26:23,130 --> 00:26:26,374
does not mean I cannot contribute
to the affairs of state.

274
00:26:26,380 --> 00:26:27,140
PRINCE SAEN THEP

275
00:26:27,174 --> 00:26:29,982
You do so, Royal Consort Sukantha,
as does my mother.

276
00:26:30,466 --> 00:26:32,333
You are both royal consorts.

277
00:26:32,361 --> 00:26:34,404
You stand as equals.

278
00:26:41,872 --> 00:26:43,280
Do not ever compare.

279
00:26:43,920 --> 00:26:45,650
Our bloodlines couldn’t be more different.

280
00:26:46,850 --> 00:26:49,180
A lady of noble birth such as myself,

281
00:26:52,330 --> 00:26:53,850
and a mere merchant’s daughter

282
00:26:56,588 --> 00:26:57,610
such as your mother,

283
00:27:00,186 --> 00:27:02,000
can never stand as equals,

284
00:27:02,960 --> 00:27:04,801
no matter how hard she fights to rise.

285
00:27:11,840 --> 00:27:12,896
Chiang La-or,

286
00:27:14,339 --> 00:27:15,801
teach your daughter better.

287
00:27:16,780 --> 00:27:18,671
Tell her that if she wishes to speak,

288
00:27:19,457 --> 00:27:21,250
she should speak with wisdom.

289
00:27:22,164 --> 00:27:24,320
Don’t simply open her mouth
and spout nonsense.

290
00:27:25,131 --> 00:27:27,450
Otherwise, everyone will learn

291
00:27:30,070 --> 00:27:31,598
that your daughter is…

292
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:34,899
an imbecile.

293
00:27:49,454 --> 00:27:50,150
My apologies—

294
00:27:50,177 --> 00:27:50,870
Jom Harn!

295
00:27:51,370 --> 00:27:52,198
Come.

296
00:28:06,910 --> 00:28:09,099
Learn to hold your tongue, Hongkham.

297
00:28:09,414 --> 00:28:10,782
Stop asking for trouble.

298
00:28:27,426 --> 00:28:29,130
I thought a war was about to break out.

299
00:28:33,310 --> 00:28:35,804
Kong Tai, you should have stepped in
to help Sean Thep.

300
00:28:38,940 --> 00:28:41,604
Fah Haam, I value my life.

301
00:28:41,795 --> 00:28:43,082
I have no wish to risk my neck.

302
00:28:44,761 --> 00:28:47,050
Did you not see the look
in Royal Consort Sukantha’s eyes?

303
00:28:47,077 --> 00:28:48,700
She could burn a man alive with it.

304
00:28:49,432 --> 00:28:51,700
If I had intervened,
I’d have been burned to ashes.

305
00:28:53,545 --> 00:28:57,902
But if we are late,
Father might burn us alive.

306
00:28:59,300 --> 00:29:00,185
You’re right, Fah Haam.

307
00:29:00,220 --> 00:29:01,032
Let’s go.

308
00:29:02,026 --> 00:29:03,198
Kong Tai!

309
00:29:04,343 --> 00:29:05,100
Goodness.

310
00:30:13,180 --> 00:30:16,290
I bow before you, Your Majesty.

311
00:31:16,320 --> 00:31:20,170
KING CHAI SAEN LUE

312
00:31:20,200 --> 00:31:22,250
SEER PHROMMAYA

313
00:31:22,280 --> 00:31:24,290
MUEN IN

314
00:31:27,256 --> 00:31:30,004
Now that you’ve returned,
I see how much you’ve grown.

315
00:31:31,400 --> 00:31:35,440
Thank you for your great support
of the Crown Prince.

316
00:31:36,880 --> 00:31:41,930
I would gladly lay down my life
for Your Majesty and the Crown Prince.

317
00:31:43,230 --> 00:31:48,472
I shall do whatever
the Crown Prince commands

318
00:31:49,894 --> 00:31:52,000
for the peace of Ullavee, Your Majesty.

319
00:31:57,340 --> 00:31:59,900
In suppressing the rebellion
along the border,

320
00:32:00,150 --> 00:32:03,890
Ullavee was at a disadvantage,
for the rebels had a far larger army.

321
00:32:04,810 --> 00:32:08,502
Yet Ullavee is guarded
by towering mountain ranges,

322
00:32:08,890 --> 00:32:11,499
making it difficult
for large armies to enter.

323
00:32:11,819 --> 00:32:13,650
Prince Indraraja recognized this advantage

324
00:32:14,250 --> 00:32:18,441
and ordered Mueang Fah and me
to lead our troops from Merng Mang

325
00:32:18,469 --> 00:32:19,970
to reinforce the army
and secure our victory.

326
00:32:20,383 --> 00:32:22,780
Prince Indraraja is truly astute.

327
00:32:24,965 --> 00:32:27,080
The enemy forces
were but untrained civilians.

328
00:32:27,395 --> 00:32:32,680
Mueang Fah and Pha Wiang,
acting under my command,

329
00:32:32,710 --> 00:32:34,050
led the troops to crush them

330
00:32:36,191 --> 00:32:38,490
and claim victory for you, Your Majesty.

331
00:32:39,776 --> 00:32:40,845
Your Majesty,

332
00:32:41,576 --> 00:32:43,302
should another rebellion arise,

333
00:32:44,333 --> 00:32:46,610
please let Jom Harn
lead the army to quell it.

334
00:32:49,681 --> 00:32:53,496
I would argue that
Saen Thep is the better choice.

335
00:32:53,880 --> 00:32:56,899
As the Third-in-Line,

336
00:32:57,145 --> 00:33:00,801
Saen Thep has fought side by side
with the Crown Prince in numerous battles.

337
00:33:01,360 --> 00:33:03,900
This is a matter
of life and death for the realm,

338
00:33:04,380 --> 00:33:06,250
not an occasion for practice.

339
00:33:08,097 --> 00:33:10,299
I agree with Royal Consort Chiang La-or.

340
00:33:11,807 --> 00:33:13,050
Jom Harn is still young.

341
00:33:15,111 --> 00:33:16,450
Which is a fair point, is it not?

342
00:33:16,737 --> 00:33:18,201
Jom Harn is young and strong.

343
00:33:18,808 --> 00:33:21,320
He is both a strategist
and a warrior in his own right.

344
00:33:21,720 --> 00:33:26,499
We need not send two men to secure
such a meager victory for His Majesty.

345
00:33:28,259 --> 00:33:35,598
Military command requires more than
youth, strength, or knowledge of warfare.

346
00:33:36,750 --> 00:33:38,666
It requires knowing
how to use one’s men wisely

347
00:33:39,103 --> 00:33:40,930
and how to read the enemy.

348
00:33:42,310 --> 00:33:43,890
Indraraja doesn’t fight himself.

349
00:33:44,514 --> 00:33:45,798
He simply makes plans…

350
00:33:48,760 --> 00:33:51,299
and orders someone else to fight for him.

351
00:33:52,854 --> 00:33:55,002
Winning through wisdom

352
00:33:55,842 --> 00:33:59,320
is more worthy of praise
than anything else.

353
00:34:01,300 --> 00:34:07,699
As things stand, no one can protect
Ullavee better than Indraraja.

354
00:34:12,820 --> 00:34:15,100
Indraraja, hear my command.

355
00:34:16,235 --> 00:34:19,601
Send troops to patrol the borders

356
00:34:20,185 --> 00:34:23,980
and ensure no further rebellions arise
to threaten Ullavee.

357
00:34:25,048 --> 00:34:27,300
I shall see to it, Your Majesty.

358
00:34:45,210 --> 00:34:47,099
Indraraja wanted to assert his dominance.

359
00:34:47,767 --> 00:34:49,630
That’s why he brought
Mueang Fah and Pha Wiang

360
00:34:49,657 --> 00:34:51,598
before Father, in front of us all.

361
00:34:52,681 --> 00:34:54,099
You’re overthinking it.

362
00:34:55,179 --> 00:34:58,970
He brought them because
they helped him with his affairs.

363
00:35:00,510 --> 00:35:02,002
You’re far too optimistic.

364
00:35:02,398 --> 00:35:05,792
Everyone knows Indraraja
never fights in battle

365
00:35:05,825 --> 00:35:07,161
or even raises a sword,

366
00:35:07,190 --> 00:35:08,801
yet he gets praised left and right.

367
00:35:10,208 --> 00:35:13,560
It’s Mueang Fah who wades through blood
on the battlefield.

368
00:35:15,280 --> 00:35:18,699
And yet Father
favors Indraraja in everything.

369
00:35:19,370 --> 00:35:20,697
He only has eyes for him.

370
00:35:22,650 --> 00:35:24,269
You keep fretting over the same matter.

371
00:35:25,327 --> 00:35:26,300
Aren’t you tired of it?

372
00:35:27,190 --> 00:35:28,248
I am.

373
00:35:29,205 --> 00:35:33,897
But I still believe you’re better suited
to devising military strategies.

374
00:35:35,671 --> 00:35:37,499
You’re the most capable among us.

375
00:35:37,859 --> 00:35:39,200
No one else comes close.

376
00:35:41,395 --> 00:35:42,930
You’re the only one who thinks so.

377
00:35:43,330 --> 00:35:45,401
Plenty of people agree with me.

378
00:35:46,979 --> 00:35:48,890
You need to make something
of yourself now.

379
00:35:49,740 --> 00:35:51,900
Once you’ve gone through
the bedding ceremony,

380
00:35:52,691 --> 00:35:54,303
you may never want to go to war again.

381
00:36:12,270 --> 00:36:14,771
Oh, whatever became of that madwoman
who interrupted our ceremony,

382
00:36:15,340 --> 00:36:17,130
Maneethip’s sister?

383
00:36:18,151 --> 00:36:19,610
Has she regained her senses yet?

384
00:36:20,410 --> 00:36:22,200
She doesn’t seem trustworthy.

385
00:36:23,100 --> 00:36:25,802
I hope she doesn’t find another chance
to sneak into the sacred spring.

386
00:37:07,180 --> 00:37:08,162
Please sit.

387
00:37:09,257 --> 00:37:10,198
Sit down, my lady.

388
00:37:17,045 --> 00:37:18,604
You mustn’t sit like this.

389
00:37:19,320 --> 00:37:20,497
It’s <i>“kued,”</i> my lady.

390
00:37:21,250 --> 00:37:22,096
<i>Kued?</i>

391
00:37:22,434 --> 00:37:23,450
What does that mean?

392
00:37:23,823 --> 00:37:25,180
It’s improper etiquette.

393
00:37:25,678 --> 00:37:30,560
It’s considered sinful, vile,
and inauspicious.

394
00:37:34,050 --> 00:37:35,602
What could be worse than that?

395
00:37:41,792 --> 00:37:46,099
Fong Nuan, you seem much healthier
and stronger than before.

396
00:37:47,672 --> 00:37:50,920
So… was I really that weak before, <i>kha</i>?

397
00:37:51,533 --> 00:37:52,360
<i>Kha?</i>

398
00:37:54,109 --> 00:37:55,177
Say, “Your Highness.”

399
00:37:56,660 --> 00:37:59,080
You must address princes
as “Your Highness.”

400
00:38:01,270 --> 00:38:02,379
“Your Highness,” it is.

401
00:38:03,280 --> 00:38:06,770
Ever since she returned from the ceremony,
she’s been acting this way.

402
00:38:07,789 --> 00:38:09,000
She speaks strangely.

403
00:38:09,840 --> 00:38:11,200
She behaves strangely.

404
00:38:11,900 --> 00:38:13,998
It’s as though her soul has left her body.

405
00:38:15,242 --> 00:38:17,690
I’d like to hold
a <i>“Hong Kwan”</i> ceremony for her.
[A traditional soul-calling ceremony]

406
00:38:18,712 --> 00:38:20,198
Let’s wait a few days.

407
00:38:21,125 --> 00:38:24,601
If she doesn’t improve,
I’ll consult <i>“Ma Khee”</i>.

408
00:38:25,630 --> 00:38:26,745
<i>Ma Khee?</i>

409
00:38:27,991 --> 00:38:29,496
<i>Ma Khee</i> is a woman

410
00:38:30,020 --> 00:38:33,330
who serves as a mediator
between the human and spirit worlds.

411
00:38:34,379 --> 00:38:37,502
When something troubles us,
when we fall ill,

412
00:38:37,900 --> 00:38:39,798
or when we lose something,

413
00:38:40,770 --> 00:38:43,810
we can seek
the spirits’ guidance through <i>Ma Khee.</i>

414
00:38:44,235 --> 00:38:45,330
Like a medium, right?

415
00:38:47,447 --> 00:38:48,728
-Medium?
-Medium?

416
00:38:52,115 --> 00:38:52,897
Uh…

417
00:38:53,711 --> 00:38:54,800
Never mind,

418
00:38:55,217 --> 00:38:56,004
Your Highness.

419
00:38:58,150 --> 00:38:59,398
So,

420
00:39:00,810 --> 00:39:02,897
why are you here, Your Highness?

421
00:39:05,442 --> 00:39:07,290
Prince Saen Thep is worried about you.

422
00:39:08,310 --> 00:39:10,097
If he hadn’t intervened

423
00:39:10,339 --> 00:39:13,490
when you sneaked into
the ceremony to honor the water spirits

424
00:39:13,880 --> 00:39:15,853
you would’ve been punished.

425
00:39:16,234 --> 00:39:17,299
Do you realize that?

426
00:39:21,330 --> 00:39:23,450
But I cannot protect you every time.

427
00:39:25,440 --> 00:39:29,201
Therefore, I forbid you
from entering that place again.

428
00:39:29,813 --> 00:39:31,280
It’s a restricted area.

429
00:39:32,010 --> 00:39:34,400
Only the King, the princes,

430
00:39:34,653 --> 00:39:38,200
and male members
of the royal family may enter.

431
00:39:39,122 --> 00:39:40,598
The place for ceremonies?

432
00:39:42,930 --> 00:39:44,672
Tell the prince you understand, Fong Nuan.

433
00:39:48,517 --> 00:39:49,299
Fong Nuan.

434
00:39:50,870 --> 00:39:54,268
Promise him
you won’t trespass there again.

435
00:39:57,220 --> 00:39:57,997
Sure.

436
00:39:59,120 --> 00:40:00,134
I won’t go, Your Highness.

437
00:42:03,896 --> 00:42:04,700
Here.

438
00:42:15,950 --> 00:42:17,496
There is no place…

439
00:42:18,700 --> 00:42:20,472
more beautiful than Ullavee.

440
00:42:21,300 --> 00:42:24,530
I know you helped Indraraja
with his affairs

441
00:42:25,150 --> 00:42:26,499
because you wanted to come home.

442
00:42:27,152 --> 00:42:28,902
You wanted to return to Ullavee.

443
00:42:31,470 --> 00:42:33,697
You seem to be the only one
who understands.

444
00:42:34,389 --> 00:42:37,610
If you mean Mother wouldn’t understand,

445
00:42:38,823 --> 00:42:40,400
then I’ll speak to her myself.

446
00:42:41,390 --> 00:42:43,700
I’ll ask her to let you live with us
in our residence.

447
00:42:45,351 --> 00:42:47,404
Then you won’t have to live
in a temple like this.

448
00:42:52,225 --> 00:42:53,890
You speak as though you don’t know Mother.

449
00:42:54,487 --> 00:42:55,400
I do.

450
00:42:56,376 --> 00:43:00,120
But I don’t understand
why she has to despise you.

451
00:43:00,703 --> 00:43:02,890
Just because you were born
in the hour of the plunderer?

452
00:43:03,490 --> 00:43:04,997
I’ve never believed in that.

453
00:43:06,069 --> 00:43:08,001
And then there’s what she told Father

454
00:43:09,060 --> 00:43:10,899
about giving me a mission to prove myself.

455
00:43:11,980 --> 00:43:13,680
I have no desire to become Crown Prince

456
00:43:14,280 --> 00:43:17,100
or inherit the throne
in Indraraja’s stead.

457
00:43:19,180 --> 00:43:23,001
I only wish to fight on the battlefield
to protect Ullavee.

458
00:43:24,130 --> 00:43:25,180
You know well

459
00:43:26,710 --> 00:43:31,099
that we can’t always do or be as we wish.

460
00:43:32,002 --> 00:43:33,045
But that can change.

461
00:43:34,090 --> 00:43:37,401
If you distinguish yourself
and earn Father’s favor,

462
00:43:38,400 --> 00:43:43,303
perhaps he’ll stop caring about the fate
foretold by the stars at your birth.

463
00:43:46,200 --> 00:43:50,568
I’d much rather
see you become Crown Prince.

464
00:43:56,266 --> 00:43:57,850
I don’t wish to become anything.

465
00:43:59,186 --> 00:44:04,100
Being your older brother
is enough to make me happy.

466
00:44:18,900 --> 00:44:20,151
Well then, next time,

467
00:44:22,120 --> 00:44:23,748
will you pull your punches a bit?

468
00:44:35,500 --> 00:44:36,346
Here.

469
00:44:48,760 --> 00:44:50,240
Indraraja had the audacity

470
00:44:50,739 --> 00:44:53,696
to bring Mueang Fah and Pha Wiang
before the King.

471
00:44:55,094 --> 00:44:57,000
One is the outcast son.

472
00:44:58,380 --> 00:45:00,250
The other is the son
of a ruler from another city.

473
00:45:00,951 --> 00:45:02,002
What was he thinking?

474
00:45:02,380 --> 00:45:03,899
How improper of him.

475
00:45:04,690 --> 00:45:10,697
Indraraja and Pha Wiang may live
in different cities, but they’re cousins.

476
00:45:10,730 --> 00:45:13,576
There’s nothing unusual about
helping each other with matters of state.

477
00:45:13,614 --> 00:45:15,000
But I don’t trust them.

478
00:45:15,546 --> 00:45:16,700
Leave us.

479
00:45:24,174 --> 00:45:25,650
Merng Mang is a border city.

480
00:45:26,620 --> 00:45:28,610
There’s no guarantee
it will remain loyal to us.

481
00:45:28,874 --> 00:45:32,290
By doing this, it’s as though
Indraraja is inviting the enemy in.

482
00:45:33,438 --> 00:45:35,210
What exactly is troubling you, Mother?

483
00:45:35,710 --> 00:45:39,090
Pha Wiang is truly clever and cunning.

484
00:45:40,485 --> 00:45:42,400
Indraraja is no better a man.

485
00:45:43,330 --> 00:45:45,271
Word among the nobles is that

486
00:45:46,484 --> 00:45:48,810
they’re extorting taxes
from caravan merchants.

487
00:45:49,850 --> 00:45:51,466
And then there’s Mueang Fah.

488
00:45:52,630 --> 00:45:54,871
He was sent to Merng Mang at a young age.

489
00:45:56,210 --> 00:45:58,248
Now he’s back in Ullavee.

490
00:45:58,917 --> 00:46:00,198
I find this peculiar.

491
00:46:03,140 --> 00:46:07,610
Do you know if those three
are plotting a rebellion?

492
00:46:09,265 --> 00:46:11,902
That’s a serious matter.
How would I know anything about that?

493
00:46:12,253 --> 00:46:14,770
You know everything.
How could you not know about this?

494
00:46:17,440 --> 00:46:18,574
Look into it.

495
00:46:18,900 --> 00:46:20,465
Find out what Indraraja is plotting.

496
00:46:20,499 --> 00:46:22,158
How am I supposed to look into it?

497
00:46:22,192 --> 00:46:23,979
Indraraja is extremely cautious.

498
00:46:24,430 --> 00:46:25,801
I can’t get close to him.

499
00:46:53,850 --> 00:46:57,580
With enemies all around me,
I must be extra cautious.

500
00:47:02,150 --> 00:47:05,872
I know many people want me dead.

501
00:47:11,706 --> 00:47:12,600
What about you?

502
00:47:14,309 --> 00:47:15,900
Are you one of them?

503
00:47:17,023 --> 00:47:18,702
I don’t want you dead.

504
00:47:19,337 --> 00:47:22,782
I want you to become King.

505
00:47:30,130 --> 00:47:36,050
Why did you bring Mueang Fah
back to Ullavee to assist you?

506
00:47:36,631 --> 00:47:38,720
Aren’t you afraid he might betray you,

507
00:47:38,988 --> 00:47:43,198
side with his mother
and his full younger brother, Jom Harn,

508
00:47:44,791 --> 00:47:47,200
and overthrow you as Crown Prince?

509
00:47:49,617 --> 00:47:51,801
Mueang Fah would never betray me.

510
00:47:52,930 --> 00:47:54,810
I know his weakness well.

511
00:47:57,660 --> 00:47:58,777
What about you?

512
00:48:00,588 --> 00:48:03,579
Don’t you wish to support Saen Thep
as my rival?

513
00:48:08,037 --> 00:48:13,401
If Saen Thep becomes King,
I shall simply be the King’s sister.

514
00:48:19,099 --> 00:48:21,001
But if you become King,

515
00:48:26,348 --> 00:48:30,320
I shall be Queen, just as we agreed.

516
00:48:35,681 --> 00:48:37,010
Aren’t you clever?

517
00:48:40,725 --> 00:48:42,299
We’re in the same boat now,

518
00:48:42,802 --> 00:48:44,930
so we must row together
to reach our destination.

519
00:48:48,310 --> 00:48:50,600
If Royal Consort Chiang La-or
and Saen Thep

520
00:48:51,229 --> 00:48:52,140
conspire to overthrow me…

521
00:48:52,160 --> 00:48:53,880
I won’t let that happen!

522
00:49:12,660 --> 00:49:14,376
Won’t you stay with me tonight?

523
00:49:15,840 --> 00:49:17,401
You can leave before dawn.

524
00:49:19,001 --> 00:49:20,250
No one will see you.

525
00:49:23,620 --> 00:49:25,702
Once you become King,

526
00:49:26,710 --> 00:49:30,899
I’ll pamper you openly,

527
00:49:31,850 --> 00:49:33,001
day…

528
00:49:37,530 --> 00:49:38,601
and night.

529
00:49:47,850 --> 00:49:51,068
You’re teasing me with every kiss.

530
00:49:58,419 --> 00:49:59,900
I mean every word.

531
00:50:48,970 --> 00:50:50,266
Now that you’re back,

532
00:50:51,510 --> 00:50:54,700
I suppose you won’t have to rush back
to Merng Mang, Prince Mueang Fah.

533
00:51:05,348 --> 00:51:07,004
Whether I stay or leave,

534
00:51:07,955 --> 00:51:10,000
do I get to decide for myself?

535
00:51:11,200 --> 00:51:12,998
You can decide everything, Your Highness.

536
00:51:14,847 --> 00:51:19,500
It all depends on
whether you choose to act.

537
00:51:30,891 --> 00:51:32,379
Since the day I was born,

538
00:51:34,586 --> 00:51:36,920
I’ve never been able to decide
anything for myself.

539
00:51:38,750 --> 00:51:43,183
The stars have dictated my fate

540
00:51:45,220 --> 00:51:47,374
since the day I came into this world.

541
00:51:51,171 --> 00:51:52,202
You’re a seer.

542
00:51:53,520 --> 00:51:56,601
You live by fate. You should know that.

543
00:52:31,782 --> 00:52:33,577
My fate…

544
00:52:36,770 --> 00:52:38,398
is to be an outcast son.

545
00:52:49,602 --> 00:52:51,202
You’ve just returned from the battlefield.

546
00:52:52,328 --> 00:52:55,170
Have you bathed in the sacred spring yet?

547
00:52:57,041 --> 00:53:02,377
Will bathing in the sacred spring
make me a beloved son?

548
00:53:04,666 --> 00:53:11,497
No matter how sacred the water is,
it cannot wash away my ill fate.

549
00:53:12,202 --> 00:53:13,774
Still, you should go

550
00:53:14,819 --> 00:53:18,960
to pay your respects and tell the spirits
you’ve returned to your homeland

551
00:53:19,970 --> 00:53:22,801
so they can protect you.

552
00:53:23,820 --> 00:53:27,771
Cleanse yourself of the enemy’s blood,

553
00:53:28,710 --> 00:53:31,851
lest evil spirits follow you.

554
00:53:39,401 --> 00:53:42,000
The stars may dictate your fate,

555
00:53:43,880 --> 00:53:47,002
but your own actions…

556
00:53:48,663 --> 00:53:51,899
can shape your life as well,
Your Highness.

557
00:54:27,773 --> 00:54:30,699
(I forbid you from entering
that place again.)

558
00:54:31,213 --> 00:54:32,690
It’s a restricted area.

559
00:54:33,423 --> 00:54:35,810
Only the King, the princes,

560
00:54:36,087 --> 00:54:39,582
and male members
of the royal family may enter.

561
00:54:40,500 --> 00:54:41,899
The place for ceremonies?

562
00:54:44,797 --> 00:54:48,202
I must go back the way I came.

563
00:55:29,800 --> 00:55:30,897
Who are you?

564
00:55:37,510 --> 00:55:38,500
I…

565
00:55:41,640 --> 00:55:43,665
I… I don’t know either.

566
00:55:44,940 --> 00:55:47,896
Do you not know this is a restricted area?

567
00:55:49,561 --> 00:55:53,979
Anyone caught sneaking in here must die.

568
00:56:02,080 --> 00:56:03,432
Well, you caught me.

569
00:56:06,325 --> 00:56:07,490
Then kill me.

570
00:56:10,611 --> 00:56:11,398
Go on.

571
00:56:12,090 --> 00:56:13,100
Kill me.

572
00:56:17,480 --> 00:56:18,837
Aren’t you afraid to die?

573
00:56:20,640 --> 00:56:22,145
There’s no point in being afraid.

574
00:56:25,234 --> 00:56:26,697
I don’t know where I am.

575
00:56:27,817 --> 00:56:29,982
I don’t know how I got here.

576
00:56:31,180 --> 00:56:33,579
I don’t know how to get back.

577
00:56:34,628 --> 00:56:36,100
I just want to go home.

578
00:56:45,238 --> 00:56:47,160
This place isn’t where I belong.

579
00:56:49,360 --> 00:56:50,900
I just want to go home!

580
00:56:52,920 --> 00:56:56,045
But there’s no one waiting for me
at home anymore.

581
00:57:03,200 --> 00:57:04,201
Kill me.

582
00:57:05,602 --> 00:57:06,897
Maybe it’s better to die!

583
00:57:13,908 --> 00:57:14,802
Go on.

584
00:57:15,337 --> 00:57:16,299
Just kill me.

585
00:57:24,810 --> 00:57:26,377
There’s no point in dying, either.

586
00:57:35,490 --> 00:57:37,143
I’ll pretend I never saw you here

587
00:57:39,040 --> 00:57:40,500
and give you your life back.

588
00:57:42,882 --> 00:57:44,699
You still have a life to live,

589
00:57:46,170 --> 00:57:47,979
so live it happily.

590
00:58:37,770 --> 00:58:40,860
You still have a life to live,
so live it happily.

591
00:58:40,893 --> 00:58:43,180
Being you isn’t so bad, Fong Nuan.

592
00:58:43,520 --> 00:58:44,157
Isn’t it pretty?

593
00:58:44,180 --> 00:58:45,610
Not pretty. You look like a madwoman.

594
00:58:45,856 --> 00:58:46,779
You’re the mad one, jerk!

595
00:58:46,810 --> 00:58:49,400
You’re quite clever, junior.

596
00:58:49,623 --> 00:58:52,240
It’s as though you and Maneethip
have switched bodies.

597
00:58:52,263 --> 00:58:53,490
Maneethip has grown quiet,

598
00:58:53,520 --> 00:58:56,200
while you never fail to make me smile.

599
00:58:56,310 --> 00:59:00,402
Anyone wishing to trade in Ullavee
must pay taxes to Crown Prince Indraraja.

600
00:59:00,600 --> 00:59:01,967
This is a grave matter, Mueang Fah.

601
00:59:02,161 --> 00:59:06,398
I saw Pha Wiang extorting protection money
from caravan merchants from Siao.

602
00:59:06,570 --> 00:59:08,794
I’d like you to see
this matter properly resolved.

603
00:59:08,820 --> 00:59:11,982
But if you have no part in this,
you would do well to be cautious.
